Subject: [PATCH 2/4] int13: room for the winrbd handoff table in the BIOS boot firmware tables

On BIOS the boot firmware tables (iBFT, aBFT, sBFT and the winrbd "rBFT" handoff table)
are copied into one fixed area, XBFTAB_SIZE bytes of data16 (src/arch/x86/interface/
pcbios/int13.c: int13_install() refuses a table that does not fit). 768 bytes
is enough for an iBFT alone; the handoff table is 152 bytes of fixed fields (36-byte ACPI header, 116-byte fixed part) plus
monitor addresses, names and, when asked for, the cephx key. 2048 bytes holds
a typical iBFT and a typical handoff table with room to spare (the largest of both together fill it exactly: see patch 0004). The cost is 1280 bytes of data16 BSS.

Licence: GPL2_OR_LATER_OR_UBDL, like the file it touches.

---
--- a/src/arch/x86/interface/pcbios/int13.c
+++ b/src/arch/x86/interface/pcbios/int13.c
@@ -1550,7 +1550,7 @@
 }
 
 /** Maximum size of boot firmware table(s) */
-#define XBFTAB_SIZE 768
+#define XBFTAB_SIZE 2048
 
 /** Alignment of boot firmware table entries */
 #define XBFTAB_ALIGN 16
